<section class="wrap sec--origin rule-top stack">
  <div class="origin__head">
    <p class="origin__word np">गोठालो</p>
    <p class="caption">go-THAA-lo. Nepali, noun: the herder.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="origin__grid">
    <p class="lede">
      The kid on the hillside with a flute and a dog, who takes the animals up to the high
      pasture in the morning and brings them back to the pen at dusk. The herd mostly looks
      after itself. The herder's whole job is to notice the one that is stuck and call it in.
      That is what this is: a small bridge and a phone app that watch every Herdr session and
      let you answer the one that bleats, without leaving your own valley.
    </p>
    <dl class="gloss">
      <dt><span class="np">गोठ</span> goth</dt>
      <dd>the pen. Where the herd comes back to at dusk, and where the bridge lives.</dd>
      <dt><span class="np">खर्क</span> kharka</dt>
      <dd>the high pasture. Herdr, where the agents graze.</dd>
      <dt><span class="np">भोटे कुकुर</span> bhote kukur</dt>
      <dd>the dog that guards and warns. It does not herd. The watcher.</dd>
      <dt><span class="np">घण्टी</span> ghanti</dt>
      <dd>the bell. A push notification.</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>
